      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2013 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
            "content": "To investigate the relationship between the resistin intronic +299G/A polymorphism and nonalcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD) in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM)."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "We selected 738 T2DM patients, including 395 with NAFLD and 343 without fatty liver disease, as well as 279 healthy control individuals, and analyzed their resistin +299G/A polymorphism genotype by polymerase chain reaction-restriction fragment length polymorphism."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "Plasma resistin levels in T2DM patients with NAFLD were at the highest (P<0.05). The frequency of AA genotype at the +299 site of the resistin gene in patients with concurrent T2DM combined with NAFLD was significantly different from that in the control (P<0.05). The AA genotype was found to be associated with a 1.80-fold increased risk for T2DM combined with NAFLD, 2.05-fold increased risk for obesity and 2.37-fold increased risk for obesity of abdominal type compared to the GG (P<0.05, respectively). The multivariate non-conditional logistic regression model analysis further shows that the AA genotype is a risk factor for the development of NAFLD in T2DM patients (OR, 2.32; 95% CI, 1.05-4.68; P<0.05)."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSION",
            "content": "The resistin +299AA genotype may be associated with increases in the risk of the NAFLD development in T2DM patients."
          }
        ]
      },
